# Next.js conventions

Stack: Next.js 16, React 19, TypeScript strict, pnpm, Tailwind 4, shadcn (base-nova), lucide, `@/` aliases.

## Structure

- Routes and metadata: `app/`
- Product UI: `components/rate-me/`
- Primitives: `components/ui/` (do not fork casually)
- Shared helpers: `lib/` (`cn` from `lib/utils.ts`)
- Keep `page.tsx` thin — compose from components.

## Server vs client

Default to Server Components. Add `'use client'` only for interactivity (nav scroll, locale toggle, rating demo, FAQ accordion).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — whole landing as one client file forever
'use client'
export default function Page() { return <EntireMarketingSite /> }

// ✅ GOOD — server page, client islands
export default function Page() {
  return <RateMeLanding />
}
```

## Metadata

Preserve `app/layout.tsx` SEO: title **Rayt Me — Verified Professional Reputation**, `metadataBase` `https://rate.me`, EN+AR keywords, JSON-LD (Organization, SoftwareApplication, FAQPage), fonts Geist + Noto Sans Arabic.

## Quality

- Prefer named exports colocated with usage; default export the page/section root.
- Do not set `typescript.ignoreBuildErrors` in new config — fix types.
- Do not add `images.unoptimized` further; prefer local `public/` assets over remote blob URLs.
- Verify UI in the browser after visual or interaction changes.
